ANCH-B-E009 | Rule 12 | Plugin provisioning produces the framework the job integration builds against; sibling edge within branch B. |\n| E002 → E005 | Rule 3 | Preemption semantics (full eviction+requeue vs checkpoint-aware) rewrites the preemption epic's scope; true gate (`rewrite`). |\n| E003 → E006 | Rule 3 | If Tech Preview topology discovery is not mature enough this release, the placement epic does not ship; true gate (`remove`). |\n| E004 → E007 | Rule 13 | The Dashboard renders the per-project quota model (quota consumption per project across job types); it builds against the quota structures E004 defines — a build-against artifact, not a configuration reference. |\n| No edge E001 → E004 | Rule 14/15 | Per-project quota is enforced by Kueue's ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model at admission under either gang-admission outcome; the investigation does not change what E004 builds. Over-serializing would block P0 quota work unnecessarily. |\n| No edges among E004, E005, E006 | Rules 1, 15 | Same component and team but distinct logical changes (quota vs preemption vs placement), different areas of the queueing configuration; parallel. |\n| No edge E001 → E007 | — | The Dashboard reads Kueue Workload CR state and queue metrics, which expose pending/admitted state under either admission mechanism; the outcome does not change the Dashboard surface. |\n| No konflux-onboarding chain | Rule 10 | All components are already in the platform and Konflux-onboarded; no pipeline onboarding epics exist, so no build-pipeline coupling edges. |\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n|---|---|---|\n| HLR-1 (all-or-nothing admission) | P0 | BRANCH-A-E008 (outcome A) or BRANCH-B-E008 + BRANCH-B-E009 (outcome B) — selected by E001 |\n| HLR-2 (per-project GPU quota at admission) | P0 | E004 |\n| HLR-3 (Dashboard queue/quota/admission visibility) | P1 | E007 |\n| HLR-4 (admin-defined preemption) | P1 | E005 (gated by E002) |\n| HLR-5 (topology-aware placement) | P2 | E006 (gated by E003) |\n\nAll five HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements. HLR-1 is covered by exactly\none branch per outcome — the branch epics are mutually exclusive alternatives,\nnot additive scope.\n\n## Priority Inheritance\n\n- E001 is P0: it gates all HLR-1 (P0) work via the branch epics.\n- E002 is P1: it gates only HLR-4 (P1).\n- E003 is P2: it gates only HLR-5 (P2).\n- E004 is P0 on its own HLR-2 merit (it also enables E007/HLR-3 at P1 — the\n  higher P0 wins).\n- Branch epics are P0 (HLR-1); they are conditional alternatives and excluded\n  from the main-plan critical path.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n1. **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): no Acceptance Criteria, NFRs,\n   Impacted Teams, or Dependencies table in the source strategy — epic ACs are\n   derived from HLRs and the problem statement; teams from architecture context.\n2. **\"Target scale\" undefined**: the strategy references \"our target scale\" for\n   gang-admission validation without quantifying it (job sizes, queue depth,\n   cluster size). E001 must pin this down before its benchmarks mean anything.\n3. **Scope trap — Tech Preview foundation (HLR-5)**: topology-aware scheduling\n   is Tech Preview per architecture context. Building a P2 placement feature on\n   it risks rework if discovery semantics change before GA; E003 gates this\n   explicitly with a remove outcome.\n4. **Schedule risk — field input for preemption**: E002 depends on reconciling\n   conflicting field/customer signals; customer availability is outside our\n   control and may delay the HLR-4 start. Noted as risk, not an AC.\n5. **Priority note**: HLR-3 (Dashboard visibility) is P1 while the queueing work\n   it visualizes is P0 — intentional per strategy, but the Dashboard epic lands\n   after quota enforcement (E004 → E007).\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable — no external dependency with uncertain timing (Kueue is already\nin-platform; the only conditional is internal approach selection, handled via\nthe branch structure above).\n\n## Conditional Branches\n\nE001 has two bounded outcomes that restructure the HLR-1 implementation:\n\n- **Outcome A — Kueue-native sufficient**: BRANCH-A-E008 configures and hardens\n  Kueue's waitForPodsReady gang admission for PyTorchJob and RayJob.\n- **Outcome B — scheduler-plugin needed**: BRANCH-B-E008 provisions a\n  coscheduling scheduler-plugin (new platform infrastructure), and\n  BRANCH-B-E009 integrates PyTorchJob/RayJob admission with it.\n\nBranch files are plan documents attached to E001, not standalone issues; main-plan\nepics do not depend on them. `epic_count` counts main-plan epics (7); branch epics\nare excluded from the critical path (main-plan critical path length: 2, e.g.\nE004 → E007).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":35671,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4ce97c1d49649e9","agent_id":"a79a016c227d57657","session_id":"e20e0106-1bbf-436d-84aa-f1899f83fce7","uuid":"e3edc76d-8782-4e1d-a87b-751489deba3b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:28:31.032Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005 into epics"}
