{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-e87951f4-9797-4a37-ba35-1614214b8249","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ef00a74f623d610","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9005-7q1kuzsz/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9005-E001.md","content":"# Validate Kueue all-or-nothing admission for multi-node training jobs\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves whether the platform's queueing system (Kueue, using\nits waitForPodsReady gang-admission semantics) satisfies the all-or-nothing\nadmission requirement for multi-node PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads at the\ntarget scale, or whether additional scheduler-plugin work (e.g. a coscheduling\nplugin) is required. The strategy flags this as the open question that \"changes\nthe shape of most implementation work\": the answer selects between a\nKueue-native configuration path and a scheduler-plugin provisioning path for\ngang admission. The deliverable is a decision document with benchmark evidence\nand a recommendation that downstream implementation planning builds on.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Quantify the target scale the validation must cover (training job sizes in\n  GPUs/pods, queue depth, cluster size, mix of PyTorchJob and RayJob), since the\n  strategy references \"our target scale\" without defining it.\n- Exercise Kueue's waitForPodsReady admission for multi-node PyTorchJob and\n  RayJob workloads at that scale: verify that pods are admitted all-or-nothing\n  and that no partial GPU occupation persists while a job waits for its\n  remaining pods.\n- Characterize failure modes: behavior when pods fail to become ready,\n  admission timeouts, node loss mid-admission, and whether partially scheduled\n  jobs release all held GPUs.\n- Assess the coscheduling scheduler-plugin alternative (upstream maturity,\n  operational cost of running a custom scheduler plugin on the platform,\n  compatibility with the existing Kueue quota model).\n- Produce a recommendation with two bounded outcomes: (A) Kueue-native\n  admission is sufficient, or (B) scheduler-plugin work is required — each with\n  an estimate of downstream implementation scope.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A documented, agreed target-scale definition (job sizes, concurrency, queue\n  depth, cluster capacity) is included in the decision document.\n- For each job type (PyTorchJob, RayJob), benchmark evidence records a\n  pass/fail result for all-or-nothing admission at target scale: either zero\n  partial GPU occupation while pending, or a documented counterexample.\n- Failure-mode behavior of waitForPodsReady (pods not ready, timeouts,\n  mid-admission node loss) is documented with observed GPU release behavior.\n- A written recommendation selects outcome A or outcome B, with rationale and\n  downstream scope implications for each rejected alternative.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0, all-or-nothing admission of multi-node training jobs): this\n  investigation gates the implementation work that delivers HLR-1; it resolves\n  which implementation approach (Kueue-native vs scheduler-plugin) is used.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":38628,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4ce97c1d49649e9","agent_id":"a79a016c227d57657","session_id":"e20e0106-1bbf-436d-84aa-f1899f83fce7","uuid":"fdbadaa2-157e-4268-8f29-fb44881240ac","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:28:52.967Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005 into epics"}
