{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-781cea97-f523-45bc-b7b1-d22a9d418d0b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae52c71a55d1bca6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9005-7q1kuzsz/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9005-E003.md","content":"# Assess topology-aware scheduling Tech Preview maturity\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation determines whether node topology discovery — currently Tech\nPreview in the platform's distributed workloads stack — is mature enough to\nbuild GPU-topology-aware placement on in this release. The strategy makes\ntopology-aligned placement (HLR-5) conditional on this maturity. The deliverable\nis a go/no-go assessment with evidence, so the placement work either proceeds\nwith a known-solid foundation or is deferred rather than built on shifting\nground.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Inventory the documented limitations of Tech Preview topology-aware\n  scheduling from upstream release notes, issue trackers, and known gaps.\n- Exercise node topology discovery on representative GPU nodes (e.g. NVLink\n  domain reporting) and verify the reported topology is accurate and stable.\n- Evaluate how the scheduler consumes topology information for placement\n  decisions and whether the integration surface is stable enough to depend on.\n- Produce a go/no-go recommendation for building topology-aligned placement in\n  this release, with a fallback (defer to a later release) if maturity is\n  insufficient.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A documented list of Tech Preview limitations with their impact on\n  topology-aware placement, each sourced from upstream documentation or issues.\n- Evidence from representative GPU nodes that discovered topology (e.g. NVLink\n  domains) matches the actual hardware topology, or a documented discrepancy.\n- A written go/no-go recommendation for this release, with explicit criteria\n  and the deferral fallback described.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-5 (P2, placement can prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes when the cluster\n  exposes topology information): this investigation gates whether the placement\n  implementation ships in this release at all.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":39962,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4ce97c1d49649e9","agent_id":"a79a016c227d57657","session_id":"e20e0106-1bbf-436d-84aa-f1899f83fce7","uuid":"df01a592-7063-4b0a-8e88-bdceaa44d976","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:29:19.290Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005 into epics"}
