{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-e49fbe50-692f-4b98-8dd8-fe9e3134019e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b27fbf34f9b9c59","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9005-7q1kuzsz/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9005-E004.md","content":"# Enforce per-project GPU quota at admission time\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic enforces per-project GPU quota at admission time across training job\ntypes (PyTorchJob and RayJob), using the queueing system's existing quota model\n(ClusterQueue/LocalQueue). Jobs whose aggregate GPU request exceeds the\nproject's quota remain pending at admission — they do not occupy GPUs — so\nover-subscription by one project cannot starve others. This delivers HLR-2 and\nis independent of which gang-admission mechanism is ultimately selected, because\nquota accounting happens at admission in either case.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Design the mapping of per-project GPU quota onto the queueing system's quota\n  primitives (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue structure, cohorts, borrowing rules).\n- Ensure quota is accounted at admission time for both PyTorchJob and RayJob\n  workloads, with GPU requests aggregated per project across job types.\n- Ensure jobs that exceed quota stay pending without holding any GPUs.\n- Provide admin-facing configuration for per-project GPU quota limits.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a project with GPU quota X, when training jobs (PyTorchJob and RayJob)\n  whose aggregate GPU request exceeds X are submitted, then the excess jobs\n  remain pending and occupy zero GPUs.\n- Given available quota within a project, when a job fitting the remaining\n  quota is submitted, then it is admitted.\n- Given jobs of both types from the same project, when quota consumption is\n  measured, then it is attributable to the project as a single aggregate.\n- Given an admin changes a project's GPU quota, when subsequent jobs are\n  admitted, then the new limit is enforced without requiring job resubmission.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0, per-project GPU quota enforced at admission time across training\n  job types): fully covered by this epic.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":40503,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4ce97c1d49649e9","agent_id":"a79a016c227d57657","session_id":"e20e0106-1bbf-436d-84aa-f1899f83fce7","uuid":"f6275acb-ed19-408a-8050-f4ebe9cab536","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:29:34.162Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005 into epics"}
