{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-1f7ffa46-1d25-46da-a050-13243f759a4d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cba1957760b2966","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9005-7q1kuzsz/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9005-E005.md","content":"# Admin-defined preemption policy for higher-priority workloads\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic implements workload preemption according to an admin-defined policy:\nwhen a higher-priority workload needs resources held by a lower-priority one,\nthe lower-priority workload is preempted per the policy and requeued. The\npreemption semantics (full eviction with requeue versus checkpoint-aware\ngraceful preemption) are determined by the preemption-semantics investigation\nthis epic is gated on; the scope below covers both possibilities, with the\ncheckpoint integration included only if that outcome is selected.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Configure workload priorities and the admin-defined preemption policy in the\n  queueing system (which priority levels may preempt which, and requeue\n  behavior of preempted workloads).\n- Ensure preempted workloads are requeued and later re-admitted when resources\n  free up, without operator intervention.\n- If checkpoint-aware graceful preemption is the selected semantics: integrate\n  checkpoint save on eviction and restore on re-admission for training jobs,\n  using the checkpoint-overhead benchmark to set sensible defaults.\n- Validate that preemption interacts correctly with per-project GPU quota\n  (preempted resources return to the project's quota pool).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an admin-defined preemption policy, when a higher-priority workload\n  requires resources held by a lower-priority workload, then the lower-priority\n  workload is preempted according to the policy.\n- Given a preempted workload, when resources become available, then it is\n  requeued and re-admitted automatically.\n- Given preemption occurs, when quota is recomputed, then the preempted\n  workload's GPU allocation is released back to its project's quota.\n- Given checkpoint-aware semantics are selected, when a workload is gracefully\n  preempted, then it resumes from its last checkpoint rather than restarting\n  (or restarts, if full-eviction semantics are selected — per the gating\n  investigation's outcome).\n- Preemption is configurable by admins (policy on/off, which priorities\n  preempt which) via supported configuration.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-4 (P1, higher-priority workloads can preempt lower-priority ones\n  according to an admin-defined policy): fully covered by this epic.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41077,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4ce97c1d49649e9","agent_id":"a79a016c227d57657","session_id":"e20e0106-1bbf-436d-84aa-f1899f83fce7","uuid":"e6556a39-946f-44db-b4cc-299f7682321b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:29:50.450Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005 into epics"}
