{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-086ecb1e-ad2a-4d0a-add3-2a76917eae22","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b380258ab0f1760e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9005-7q1kuzsz/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9005-E006.md","content":"# Topology-aware GPU placement preference\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic makes job placement prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes when the\ncluster exposes topology information, addressing the throughput loss reported\nwhen training jobs land on pods crossing NVLink domains. It is gated on the\ntopology-maturity assessment: it only proceeds in this release if node topology\ndiscovery (currently Tech Preview) is judged mature enough to build on; if not,\nthis epic is removed from the release plan and deferred.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Consume node topology information (e.g. NVLink domains) exposed by the\n  cluster's topology discovery, per the maturity assessment's findings.\n- Implement placement preference so that a training job's GPU allocation is\n  topology-aligned where possible (pods placed within aligned topology domains).\n- Ensure graceful fallback: when the cluster does not expose topology\n  information, placement falls back to default scheduling behavior with no\n  degradation.\n- Keep the behavior a preference, not a hard requirement — jobs must still be\n  schedulable when perfectly aligned placement is impossible.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a cluster exposing topology information, when a multi-node training job\n  is placed, then its pods are placed on topology-aligned nodes according to\n  the preference policy.\n- Given a cluster that does not expose topology information, when a job is\n  scheduled, then placement falls back to default behavior and the job still\n  runs.\n- Given aligned placement is impossible (fragmented topology), when a job is\n  scheduled, then it is still admitted rather than blocked.\n- Given topology-aligned versus non-aligned placements of a representative\n  job, when throughput is compared, then the aligned placement shows the\n  expected improvement (validating the feature does what it exists for).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-5 (P2, job placement can prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes when the\n  cluster exposes topology information): fully covered by this epic.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41734,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4ce97c1d49649e9","agent_id":"a79a016c227d57657","session_id":"e20e0106-1bbf-436d-84aa-f1899f83fce7","uuid":"36f54551-a2e5-4f57-a7ef-4d0b15081377","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:30:04.613Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005 into epics"}
