{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-a895579d-0097-4349-924f-258486ea297f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-87b726a45dcc67de","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9005-7q1kuzsz/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E008.md","content":"# Kueue-native gang admission configuration for multi-node training jobs\n\n## Description\n\nThis branch epic delivers all-or-nothing (gang) admission of multi-node\ntraining jobs using the platform's existing queueing system, taken in the\noutcome where the gang-admission validation concluded that Kueue's\nwaitForPodsReady semantics are sufficient at target scale. It configures and\nhardens Kueue gang admission so that a multi-node job either gets all its pods\nand GPUs at once or holds nothing — no partial GPU occupation while waiting for\nremaining pods, and no partially scheduled jobs dying on timeout.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Configure all-or-nothing admission semantics for multi-node PyTorchJob and\n  RayJob workloads in the queueing system, per the validation's findings.\n- Ensure admission timeouts evict the entire partial allocation (all pods,\n  all GPUs) and requeue the job, so stranded partial allocations cannot occur.\n- Verify workload integration for both job types: job pods are held until the\n  full gang can be admitted.\n- Validate that training jobs run correctly under gang admission (the Training\n  Operator component requires no code change; its jobs must keep working — this\n  is a validation acceptance criterion, not an implementation surface).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a multi-node job requiring N GPUs, when only M < N GPUs are available,\n  then the job holds zero GPUs while pending (no partial occupation).\n- Given enough GPUs become available, when the job is admitted, then all of\n  its pods start together as one unit.\n- Given a job's pods fail to become ready within the admission timeout, when\n  the timeout fires, then the entire partial allocation is released and the job\n  is requeued.\n- Given PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads, when run under gang admission, then\n  both job types complete correctly (Training Operator passive validation).\n- Given mixed fleets with other teams' jobs queued, when a large job waits for\n  its full gang, then it does not starve other queues beyond configured\n  policy.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0, multi-node training jobs are admitted all-or-nothing: no partial\n  GPU occupation while waiting for remaining pods): fully covered by this epic\n  in outcome A (Kueue-native admission sufficient).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":42914,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4ce97c1d49649e9","agent_id":"a79a016c227d57657","session_id":"e20e0106-1bbf-436d-84aa-f1899f83fce7","uuid":"054f413c-3bf7-4785-910d-2a457d0033d2","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:30:35.022Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005 into epics"}
