e entire partial allocation is released and the\n  job is requeued.\n- Given both job types running under plugin-based gang admission, when jobs\n  complete, then training results are correct (Training Operator validation;\n  operator-side changes, if any, are included in this scope).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0, multi-node training jobs are admitted all-or-nothing: no partial\n  GPU occupation while waiting for remaining pods): completes HLR-1 coverage in\n  outcome B, building on the scheduler-plugin provisioning epic in this branch.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44229,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4ce97c1d49649e9","agent_id":"a79a016c227d57657","session_id":"e20e0106-1bbf-436d-84aa-f1899f83fce7","uuid":"8fe0ffcc-fbb3-471e-89f1-94dcbc4a134d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:31:02.846Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005 into epics"}
