epends on reconciling\n150\t   conflicting field/customer signals; customer availability is outside our\n151\t   control and may delay the HLR-4 start. Noted as risk, not an AC.\n152\t5. **Priority note**: HLR-3 (Dashboard visibility) is P1 while the queueing work\n153\t   it visualizes is P0 — intentional per strategy, but the Dashboard epic lands\n154\t   after quota enforcement (E004 → E007).\n155\t\n156\t## Tiered Delivery\n157\t\n158\tNot applicable — no external dependency with uncertain timing (Kueue is already\n159\tin-platform; the only conditional is internal approach selection, handled via\n160\tthe branch structure above).\n161\t\n162\t## Conditional Branches\n163\t\n164\tE001 has two bounded outcomes that restructure the HLR-1 implementation:\n165\t\n166\t- **Outcome A — Kueue-native sufficient**: BRANCH-A-E008 configures and hardens\n167\t  Kueue's waitForPodsReady gang admission for PyTorchJob and RayJob.\n168\t- **Outcome B — scheduler-plugin needed**: BRANCH-B-E008 provisions a\n169\t  coscheduling scheduler-plugin (new platform infrastructure), and\n170\t  BRANCH-B-E009 integrates PyTorchJob/RayJob admission with it.\n171\t\n172\tBranch files are plan documents attached to E001, not standalone issues; main-plan\n173\tepics do not depend on them. `epic_count` counts main-plan epics (7); branch epics\n174\tare excluded from the critical path (main-plan critical path length: 2, e.g.\n175\tE004 → E007).\n176\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9850fdc7d99bd18f","agent_id":"a3984109486a77230","session_id":"e20e0106-1bbf-436d-84aa-f1899f83fce7","uuid":"b245e72a-f5ed-491a-bccd-770bffb399f7","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:36:15.825Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae2450a72063b996","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
