{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfec02bd2e2abafe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E004\n3\ttitle: Enforce per-project GPU quota at admission time\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Enforce per-project GPU quota at admission time\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic enforces per-project GPU quota at admission time across training job\n34\ttypes (PyTorchJob and RayJob), using the queueing system's existing quota model\n35\t(ClusterQueue/LocalQueue). Jobs whose aggregate GPU request exceeds the\n36\tproject's quota remain pending at admission — they do not occupy GPUs — so\n37\tover-subscription by one project cannot starve others. This delivers HLR-2 and\n38\tis independent of which gang-admission mechanism is ultimately selected, because\n39\tquota accounting happens at admission in either case.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Design the mapping of per-project GPU quota onto the queueing system's quota\n44\t  primitives (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue structure, cohorts, borrowing rules).\n45\t- Ensure quota is accounted at admission time for both PyTorchJob and RayJob\n46\t  workloads, with GPU requests aggregated per project across job types.\n47\t- Ensure jobs that exceed quota stay pending without holding any GPUs.\n48\t- Provide admin-facing configuration for per-project GPU quota limits.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- Given a project with GPU quota X, when training jobs (PyTorchJob and RayJob)\n53\t  whose aggregate GPU request exceeds X are submitted, then the excess jobs\n54\t  remain pending and occupy zero GPUs.\n55\t- Given available quota within a project, when a job fitting the remaining\n56\t  quota is submitted, then it is admitted.\n57\t- Given jobs of both types from the same project, when quota consumption is\n58\t  measured, then it is attributable to the project as a single aggregate.\n59\t- Given an admin changes a project's GPU quota, when subsequent jobs are\n60\t  admitted, then the new limit is enforced without requiring job resubmission.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-2 (P0, per-project GPU quota enforced at admission time across training\n65\t  job types): fully covered by this epic.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9850fdc7d99bd18f","agent_id":"a3984109486a77230","session_id":"e20e0106-1bbf-436d-84aa-f1899f83fce7","uuid":"a8e015d1-8a2c-40e9-a194-16c2caff7c9b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:36:27.325Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfec02bd2e2abafe","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
