{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc50053e83543d02","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E006\n3\ttitle: Topology-aware GPU placement preference\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E003\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E003\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: remove\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the Tech Preview topology discovery is not mature enough for\n15\t    this release, remove this epic from the release plan and defer topology-aware\n16\t    placement to a later release.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 0\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Medium\n30\tai_implementability_score: 1\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Topology-aware GPU placement preference\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic makes job placement prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes when the\n39\tcluster exposes topology information, addressing the throughput loss reported\n40\twhen training jobs land on pods crossing NVLink domains. It is gated on the\n41\ttopology-maturity assessment: it only proceeds in this release if node topology\n42\tdiscovery (currently Tech Preview) is judged mature enough to build on; if not,\n43\tthis epic is removed from the release plan and deferred.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Consume node topology information (e.g. NVLink domains) exposed by the\n48\t  cluster's topology discovery, per the maturity assessment's findings.\n49\t- Implement placement preference so that a training job's GPU allocation is\n50\t  topology-aligned where possible (pods placed within aligned topology domains).\n51\t- Ensure graceful fallback: when the cluster does not expose topology\n52\t  information, placement falls back to default scheduling behavior with no\n53\t  degradation.\n54\t- Keep the behavior a preference, not a hard requirement — jobs must still be\n55\t  schedulable when perfectly aligned placement is impossible.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- Given a cluster exposing topology information, when a multi-node training job\n60\t  is placed, then its pods are placed on topology-aligned nodes according to\n61\t  the preference policy.\n62\t- Given a cluster that does not expose topology information, when a job is\n63\t  scheduled, then placement falls back to default behavior and the job still\n64\t  runs.\n65\t- Given aligned placement is impossible (fragmented topology), when a job is\n66\t  scheduled, then it is still admitted rather than blocked.\n67\t- Given topology-aligned versus non-aligned placements of a representative\n68\t  job, when throughput is compared, then the aligned placement shows the\n69\t  expected improvement (validating the feature does what it exists for).\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-5 (P2, job placement can prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes when the\n74\t  cluster exposes topology information): fully covered by this epic.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9850fdc7d99bd18f","agent_id":"a3984109486a77230","session_id":"e20e0106-1bbf-436d-84aa-f1899f83fce7","uuid":"1f68e0ce-b041-468c-81b1-9dbe3d81fc73","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:36:29.386Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc50053e83543d02","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
