{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac147de4018fb301","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E007\n3\ttitle: Dashboard visibility into queue position, quota, and admission state\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E004\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Dashboard visibility into queue position, quota, and admission state\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic gives users visibility into their pending distributed training jobs\n35\tin the Dashboard: queue position, per-project GPU quota consumption, and\n36\tadmission state. Users currently cannot see why a job is pending or how much\n37\tquota it consumes; this epic surfaces the queueing state that the platform's\n38\tadmission and quota enforcement produce. It builds on the per-project quota\n39\tmodel (the quota structures whose consumption it displays) and reads workload\n40\tadmission state and queue metrics exposed by the queueing system.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Add Dashboard surface (view/section) listing pending distributed workloads\n45\t  with their queue position, admission state (pending/admitted), and per-project\n46\t  GPU quota consumption.\n47\t- Read queue and workload state from the queueing system's Kubernetes CRs\n48\t  (Workload) and its exposed queue metrics; the Dashboard owns no data plane.\n49\t- Gate the new surface behind the Dashboard's existing per-component feature\n50\t  flag mechanism (OdhDashboardConfig).\n51\t- Keep existing distributed workload status views unaffected.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- Given a pending training job, when the user opens the Dashboard, then the\n56\t  job's queue position, admission state, and its project's quota consumption\n57\t  are displayed.\n58\t- Given a job transitions from pending to admitted, when the Dashboard view is\n59\t  refreshed, then the admission state shown matches the queueing system's\n60\t  actual state.\n61\t- Given the feature flag is disabled, when the Dashboard is loaded, then the\n62\t  new surface is hidden and existing views are unchanged.\n63\t- Given workloads from multiple projects, when a user views quota consumption,\n64\t  then only their project's consumption is shown (project-scoped RBAC\n65\t  respected).\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-3 (P1, users can see queue position, quota consumption, and admission\n70\t  state for their pending jobs in the Dashboard): fully covered by this epic.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9850fdc7d99bd18f","agent_id":"a3984109486a77230","session_id":"e20e0106-1bbf-436d-84aa-f1899f83fce7","uuid":"07c86444-f20a-4685-b94d-89005e8eeb21","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:36:30.558Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac147de4018fb301","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
