{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e5deeb3f3fc6683","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E008\n3\ttitle: Kueue-native gang admission configuration for multi-node training jobs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If validation shows Kueue-native admission is insufficient at\n16\t    target scale, this work is rewritten onto the scheduler-plugin path (provision\n17\t    coscheduling plugin and integrate job workloads with it).\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: 1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 8\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Kueue-native gang admission configuration for multi-node training jobs\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis branch epic delivers all-or-nothing (gang) admission of multi-node\n39\ttraining jobs using the platform's existing queueing system, taken in the\n40\toutcome where the gang-admission validation concluded that Kueue's\n41\twaitForPodsReady semantics are sufficient at target scale. It configures and\n42\thardens Kueue gang admission so that a multi-node job either gets all its pods\n43\tand GPUs at once or holds nothing — no partial GPU occupation while waiting for\n44\tremaining pods, and no partially scheduled jobs dying on timeout.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Configure all-or-nothing admission semantics for multi-node PyTorchJob and\n49\t  RayJob workloads in the queueing system, per the validation's findings.\n50\t- Ensure admission timeouts evict the entire partial allocation (all pods,\n51\t  all GPUs) and requeue the job, so stranded partial allocations cannot occur.\n52\t- Verify workload integration for both job types: job pods are held until the\n53\t  full gang can be admitted.\n54\t- Validate that training jobs run correctly under gang admission (the Training\n55\t  Operator component requires no code change; its jobs must keep working — this\n56\t  is a validation acceptance criterion, not an implementation surface).\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Given a multi-node job requiring N GPUs, when only M < N GPUs are available,\n61\t  then the job holds zero GPUs while pending (no partial occupation).\n62\t- Given enough GPUs become available, when the job is admitted, then all of\n63\t  its pods start together as one unit.\n64\t- Given a job's pods fail to become ready within the admission timeout, when\n65\t  the timeout fires, then the entire partial allocation is released and the job\n66\t  is requeued.\n67\t- Given PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads, when run under gang admission, then\n68\t  both job types complete correctly (Training Operator passive validation).\n69\t- Given mixed fleets with other teams' jobs queued, when a large job waits for\n70\t  its full gang, then it does not starve other queues beyond configured\n71\t  policy.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-1 (P0, multi-node training jobs are admitted all-or-nothing: no partial\n76\t  GPU occupation while waiting for remaining pods): fully covered by this epic\n77\t  in outcome A (Kueue-native admission sufficient).\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9850fdc7d99bd18f","agent_id":"a3984109486a77230","session_id":"e20e0106-1bbf-436d-84aa-f1899f83fce7","uuid":"310418f0-2352-4a53-a20d-483c0de5f6e1","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:36:41.836Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e5deeb3f3fc6683","permi