{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-801d30eaf7e0fb33","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E009\n3\ttitle: Gang admission integration for training jobs via scheduler plugin\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E008\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If job-type integration with the scheduler plugin is not feasible\n17\t    for both PyTorchJob and RayJob, rewrite to per-job-type fallbacks or return to\n18\t    the Kueue-native admission path for the affected job types.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: 0\n25\t  external_dependency: -1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 0\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 2\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Gang admission integration for training jobs via scheduler plugin\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis branch epic integrates multi-node training workloads (PyTorchJob and\n40\tRayJob) with the coscheduling scheduler-plugin provisioned earlier in this\n41\tbranch, so that training jobs are admitted all-or-nothing: a job either gets\n42\tits full pod set and GPUs at once or holds nothing. It is the outcome-B\n43\tcounterpart of the queueing-system configuration work, taken when the\n44\tgang-admission validation concluded that scheduler-plugin support is required.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Integrate PyTorchJob workloads with the scheduler plugin's pod-group\n49\t  semantics so job pods are scheduled as one gang (may require\n50\t  training-operator-side changes to emit the required pod-group markings).\n51\t- Integrate RayJob workloads with the same gang semantics.\n52\t- Keep per-project GPU quota enforced at admission with the plugin active\n53\t  (quota accounting must survive the change of admission mechanism).\n54\t- Validate end-to-end behavior for both job types, including admission\n55\t  timeouts releasing the entire partial allocation.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- Given a PyTorchJob requiring N GPUs, when only M < N GPUs are available,\n60\t  then the job holds zero GPUs while pending.\n61\t- Given a RayJob with a multi-node actor/worker topology, when its full gang\n62\t  cannot be admitted, then no partial allocation is held.\n63\t- Given the scheduler plugin is active, when jobs are admitted, then\n64\t  per-project GPU quota is still enforced at admission time.\n65\t- Given a job's pods fail to become ready within the admission timeout, when\n66\t  the timeout fires, then the entire partial allocation is released and the\n67\t  job is requeued.\n68\t- Given both job types running under plugin-based gang admission, when jobs\n69\t  complete, then training results are correct (Training Operator validation;\n70\t  operator-side changes, if any, are included in this scope).\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- HLR-1 (P0, multi-node training jobs are admitted all-or-nothing: no partial\n75\t  GPU occupation while waiting for remaining pods): completes HLR-1 coverage in\n76\t  outcome B, building on the scheduler-plugin provisioning epic in this branch.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3f42b40919e63c4","agent_id":"a15653fdf087f4c81","session_id":"e20e0106-1bbf-436d-84aa-f1899f83fce7","uuid":"7c759db8-a57f-49e1-939c-efc3f4171a87","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:41:56.982Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-801d30eaf7e0fb33","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
