istributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | Active (Kueue queueing, quota, preemption, placement) |\n37\t| Training Operator | Training Operator | Distributed Workloads | Passive for the Kueue-native path (no code change; jobs must keep working — validation ACs on the gang-admission epics). May become active if the scheduler-plugin branch is selected; that work is inside the branch scope. |\n38\t| Dashboard | Dashboard | RHOAI Dashboard | Active (HLR-3 visibility UI) |\n39\t\n40\tAll epic `component` values are verbatim canonical names from\n41\t`.context/rhai-components.txt`. The scheduler-plugin integration epic\n42\t(BRANCH-B-E009) spans Training Operator (PyTorchJob) and KubeRay (RayJob)\n43\tsurfaces; it is assigned `Distributed Workloads` as the single most-relevant\n44\tcanonical name for the scheduling stack, with the span noted here.\n45\t\n46\t## Epic List\n47\t\n48\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n49\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n50\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E001 | Validate Kueue all-or-nothing admission for multi-node training jobs | Investigation | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n51\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E002 | Determine required preemption semantics and checkpoint overhead | Investigation | Distributed Workloads | P1 |\n52\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E003 | Assess topology-aware scheduling Tech Preview maturity | Investigation | Distributed Workloads | P2 |\n53\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E004 | Enforce per-project GPU quota at admission time | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n54\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E005 | Admin-defined preemption policy for higher-priority workloads | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P1 |\n55\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E006 | Topology-aware GPU placement preference | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P2 |\n56\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E007 | Dashboard visibility into queue position, quota, and admission state | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n57\t\n58\tConditional branch epics (attached to E001 as plan document, not standalone issues):\n59\t\n60\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n61\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n62\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E008 | Kueue-native gang admission configuration for multi-node training jobs | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n63\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E008 | Provision coscheduling scheduler-plugin for gang scheduling | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n64\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E009 | Gang admission integration for training jobs via scheduler plugin | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n65\t\n66\t## Dependency DAG (main plan)\n67\t\n68\t```mermaid\n69\tgraph TD\n70\t    E001[\"E001 Validate gang admission semantics (Investigation)\"]\n71\t    E002[\"E002 Preemption semantics investigation\"]\n72\t    E003[\"E003 Topology TP maturity investigation\"]\n73\t    E004[\"E004 Per-project GPU quota enforcement\"]\n74\t    E005[\"E005 Preemption policy implementation\"]\n75\t    E006[\"E006 Topology-aware placement\"]\n76\t    E007[\"E007 Dashboard queue/quota/admission visibility\"]\n77\t    E002 --> E005\n78\t    E003 --> E006\n79\t    E004 --> E007\n80\t```\n81\t\n82\tBranch DAG (conditional, gated by E001; excluded from the main-plan critical path):\n83\t\n84\t```mermaid\n85\tgraph TD\n86\t    E001[\"E001 Validate gang admission semantics\"]\n87\t    BA[\"BRANCH-A-E008 Kueue-native gang admission (outcome A)\"]\n88\t    BB1[\"BRANCH-B-E008 Provision coscheduling plugin (outcome B)\"]\n89\t    BB2[\"BRANCH-B-E009 Job integration via plugin (outcome B)\"]\n90\t    E001 --> BA\n91\t    E001 --> BB1\n92\t    E001 --> BB2\n93\t    BB1 --> BB2\n94\t```\n95\t\n96\t## DAG Justification\n97\t\n98\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n99\t|---|---|---|\n100\t| E001 → BRANCH-A-E008 | Rule 3 | Gang-admission validation selects the implementation approach; true gate (`rewrite`). Bounded outcomes (Kueue-native sufficient vs scheduler-plugin needed) → conditional branches. |\n101\t| E001 → BRANCH-B-E008 | Rules 3, 22 | If Kueue is insufficient, the coscheduling scheduler-plugin is new infrastructure not in the platform inventory → provisioning epic gated on the validation outcome. |\n102\t| E001 → BRANCH-B-E009 | Rule 3 | Job-type integration only exists in the plugin outcome; gated on the same validation. |\n103\t| BRANCH-B-E008 → BRANCH-B-E009 | Rule 12 | Plugin provisioning produces the framework the job integration builds against; sibling edge within branch B. |\n104\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 3 | Preemption semantics (full eviction+requeue vs checkpoint-aware) rewrites the preemption epic's scope; true gate (`rewrite`). |\n105\t| E003 → E006 | Rule 3 | If Tech Preview topology discovery is not mature enough this release, the placement epic does not ship; true gate (`remove`). |\n106\t| E004 → E007 | Rule 13 | The Dashboard renders the per-project quota model (quota consumption per project across job types); it builds against the quota structures E004 defines — a build-against artifact, not a configuration reference. |\n107\t| No edge E001 → E004 | Rule 14/15 | Per-project quota is enforced by Kueue's ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model at admission under either gang-admission outcome; the investigation does not change what E004 builds. Over-serializing would block P0 quota work unnecessarily. |\n108\t| No edges among E004, E005, E006 | Rules 1, 15 | Same component and team but distinct logical changes (quota vs preemption vs placement), different areas of the queueing configuration; parallel. |\n109\t| No edge E001 → E007 | — | The Dashboard reads Kueue Workload CR state and queue metrics, which expose pending/admitted state under either admission mechanism; the outcome does not change the Dashboard surface. |\n110\t| No konflux-onboarding chain | Rule 10 | All components are already in the platform and Konflux-onboarded; no pipeline onboarding epics exist, so no build-pipeline coupling edges. |\n111\t\n112\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n113\t\n114\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n115\t|---|---|---|\n116\t| HLR-1 (all-or-nothing admission) | P0 | BRANCH-A-E008 (outcome A) or BRANCH-B-E008 + BRANCH-B-E009 (outcome B) — selected by E001 |\n117\t| HLR-2 (per-project GPU quota at admission) | P0 | E004 |\n118\t| HLR-3 (Dashboard queue/quota/admission visibility) | P1 | E007 |\n119\t| HLR-4 (admin-defined preemption) | P1 | E005 (gated by E002) |\n120\t| HLR-5 (topology-aware placement) | P2 | E006 (gated by E003) |\n121\t\n122\tAll five HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements. HLR-1 is covered by exactly\n123\tone branch per outcome — the branch epics are mutually exclusive alternatives,\n124\tnot additive scope.\n125\t\n126\t## Priority Inheritance\n127\t\n128\t- E001 is P0: it gates all HLR-1 (P0) work via the branch epics.\n129\t- E002 is P1: it gates only HLR-4 (P1).\n130\t- E003 is P2: it gates only HLR-5 (P2).\n131\t- E004 is P0 on its own HLR-2 merit (it also enables E007/HLR-3 at P1 — the\n132\t  higher P0 wins).\n133\t- Branch epics are P0 (HLR-1); they are conditional alternatives and excluded\n134\t  from the main-plan critical path.\n135\t\n136\t## Health Warnings\n137\t\n138\t1. **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): no Acceptance Criteria, NFRs,\n139\t   Impacted Teams, or Dependencies table in the source strategy — epic ACs are\n140\t   derived from HLRs and the problem statement; teams from architecture context.\n141\t2. **\"Target scale\" undefined**: the strategy references \"our target scale\" for\n142\t   gang-admission validation without quantifying it (job sizes, queue depth,\n143\t   cluster size). E001 must pin this down before its benchmarks mean anything.\n144\t3. **Scope trap — Tech Preview foundation (HLR-5)**: topology-aware scheduling\n145\t   is Tech Preview per architecture context. Building a P2 placement feature on\n146\t   it risks rework if discovery semantics change before GA; E003 gates this\n147\t   explicitly with a remove outcome.\n148\t4. **Schedule risk — field input for preemption**: E002 depends on reconciling\n149\t   conflicting field/customer signals; customer availability is outside our\n150\t   control and may delay the HLR-4 start. Noted as risk, not an AC.\n151\t5. **Priority note**: HLR-3 (Dashboard visibility) is P1 while the queueing work\n152\t   it visualizes is P0 — intentional per strategy, but the Dashboard epic lands\n153\t   after quota enforcement (E004 → E007).\n154\t\n155\t## Tiered Delivery\n156\t\n157\tNot applicable — no external dependency with uncertain timing (Kueue is already\n158\tin-platform; the only conditional is internal approach selection, handled via\n159\tthe branch structure above).\n160\t\n161\t## Conditional Branches\n162\t\n163\tE001 has two bounded outcomes that restructure the HLR-1 implementation:\n164\t\n165\t- **Outcome A — Kueue-native sufficient**: BRANCH-A-E008 configures and hardens\n166\t  Kueue's waitForPodsReady gang admission for PyTorchJob and RayJob.\n167\t- **Outcome B — scheduler-plugin needed**: BRANCH-B-E008 provisions a\n168\t  coscheduling scheduler-plugin (new platform infrastructure), and\n169\t  BRANCH-B-E009 integrates PyTorchJob/RayJob admission with it.\n170\t\n171\tBranch files are plan documents attached to E001, not standalone issues; main-plan\n172\tepics do not depend on them. `epic_count` counts main-plan epics (7); branch epics\n173\tare excluded from the critical path (main-plan critical path length: 2, e.g.\n174\tE004 → E007).\n175\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3f42b40919e63c4","agent_id":"a15653fdf087f4c81","session_id":"e20e0106-1bbf-436d-84aa-f1899f83fce7","uuid":"f149e197-9de3-4eda-a8af-02d402a165da","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:42:06.010Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-98b2b2f74e7a0909","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
