{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-95c9836ca57d98ae","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n3\ttitle: Validate Kueue all-or-nothing admission for multi-node training jobs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Validate Kueue all-or-nothing admission for multi-node training jobs\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves whether the platform's queueing system (Kueue, using\n30\tits waitForPodsReady gang-admission semantics) satisfies the all-or-nothing\n31\tadmission requirement for multi-node PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads at the\n32\ttarget scale, or whether additional scheduler-plugin work (e.g. a coscheduling\n33\tplugin) is required. The strategy flags this as the open question that \"changes\n34\tthe shape of most implementation work\": the answer selects between a\n35\tKueue-native configuration path and a scheduler-plugin provisioning path for\n36\tgang admission. The deliverable is a decision document with benchmark evidence\n37\tand a recommendation that downstream implementation planning builds on.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Quantify the target scale the validation must cover (training job sizes in\n42\t  GPUs/pods, queue depth, cluster size, mix of PyTorchJob and RayJob), since the\n43\t  strategy references \"our target scale\" without defining it.\n44\t- Exercise Kueue's waitForPodsReady admission for multi-node PyTorchJob and\n45\t  RayJob workloads at that scale: verify that pods are admitted all-or-nothing\n46\t  and that no partial GPU occupation persists while a job waits for its\n47\t  remaining pods.\n48\t- Characterize failure modes: behavior when pods fail to become ready,\n49\t  admission timeouts, node loss mid-admission, and whether partially scheduled\n50\t  jobs release all held GPUs.\n51\t- Assess the coscheduling scheduler-plugin alternative (upstream maturity,\n52\t  operational cost of running a custom scheduler plugin on the platform,\n53\t  compatibility with the existing Kueue quota model).\n54\t- Produce a recommendation with two bounded outcomes: (A) Kueue-native\n55\t  admission is sufficient, or (B) scheduler-plugin work is required — each with\n56\t  an estimate of downstream implementation scope.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- A documented, agreed target-scale definition (job sizes, concurrency, queue\n61\t  depth, cluster capacity) is included in the decision document.\n62\t- For each job type (PyTorchJob, RayJob), benchmark evidence records a\n63\t  pass/fail result for all-or-nothing admission at target scale: either zero\n64\t  partial GPU occupation while pending, or a documented counterexample.\n65\t- Failure-mode behavior of waitForPodsReady (pods not ready, timeouts,\n66\t  mid-admission node loss) is documented with observed GPU release behavior.\n67\t- A written recommendation selects outcome A or outcome B, with rationale and\n68\t  downstream scope implications for each rejected alternative.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- HLR-1 (P0, all-or-nothing admission of multi-node training jobs): this\n73\t  investigation gates the implementation work that delivers HLR-1; it resolves\n74\t  which implementation approach (Kueue-native vs scheduler-plugin) is used.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b03e3fa461f4ed78","agent_id":"a0b58cf02cca6a57f","session_id":"e20e0106-1bbf-436d-84aa-f1899f83fce7","uuid":"86e798c8-c714-4a9a-8274-7b3d6edab689","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:44:03.550Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-95c9836ca57d98ae","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
