{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b737eaf4998379ee","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E003\n3\ttitle: Assess topology-aware scheduling Tech Preview maturity\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Assess topology-aware scheduling Tech Preview maturity\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation determines whether node topology discovery — currently Tech\n30\tPreview in the platform's distributed workloads stack — is mature enough to\n31\tbuild GPU-topology-aware placement on in this release. The strategy makes\n32\ttopology-aligned placement (HLR-5) conditional on this maturity. The deliverable\n33\tis a go/no-go assessment with evidence, so the placement work either proceeds\n34\twith a known-solid foundation or is deferred rather than built on shifting\n35\tground.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Inventory the documented limitations of Tech Preview topology-aware\n40\t  scheduling from upstream release notes, issue trackers, and known gaps.\n41\t- Exercise node topology discovery on representative GPU nodes (e.g. NVLink\n42\t  domain reporting) and verify the reported topology is accurate and stable.\n43\t- Evaluate how the scheduler consumes topology information for placement\n44\t  decisions and whether the integration surface is stable enough to depend on.\n45\t- Produce a go/no-go recommendation for building topology-aligned placement in\n46\t  this release, with a fallback (defer to a later release) if maturity is\n47\t  insufficient.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- A documented list of Tech Preview limitations with their impact on\n52\t  topology-aware placement, each sourced from upstream documentation or issues.\n53\t- Evidence from representative GPU nodes that discovered topology (e.g. NVLink\n54\t  domains) matches the actual hardware topology, or a documented discrepancy.\n55\t- A written go/no-go recommendation for this release, with explicit criteria\n56\t  and the deferral fallback described.\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- HLR-5 (P2, placement can prefer GPU-topology-aligned nodes when the cluster\n61\t  exposes topology information): this investigation gates whether the placement\n62\t  implementation ships in this release at all.\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b03e3fa461f4ed78","agent_id":"a0b58cf02cca6a57f","session_id":"e20e0106-1bbf-436d-84aa-f1899f83fce7","uuid":"76f6a76c-9b4b-4f00-a1c5-19a7e32b7766","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:44:05.715Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b737eaf4998379ee","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
