{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae1aa398148a75fb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E008\n3\ttitle: Provision coscheduling scheduler-plugin for gang scheduling\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the scheduler-plugin approach proves unmanageable on the platform,\n16\t    fall back to the Kueue-native configuration path and harden its admission semantics\n17\t    instead.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 0\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: -1\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 0\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Low\n31\tai_implementability_score: -1\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Provision coscheduling scheduler-plugin for gang scheduling\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis branch epic provisions a coscheduling scheduler-plugin as new scheduling\n39\tinfrastructure for the platform, taken in the outcome where the gang-admission\n40\tvalidation concluded that the queueing system's native waitForPodsReady\n41\tsemantics are insufficient at target scale. The plugin is not currently shipped\n42\tin the platform, so this epic covers its packaging, deployment, and basic\n43\tvalidation as gang-scheduling infrastructure; the job-type integration that\n44\tbuilds on it is a separate epic within this branch.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Select and package the coscheduling scheduler-plugin for the platform\n49\t  (midstream fork under the platform's orgs, per the platform's midstream\n50\t  conventions).\n51\t- Deploy the plugin so it runs alongside the existing scheduler without\n52\t  disrupting default scheduling for non-gang workloads.\n53\t- Integrate its deployment with the platform's component management so it can\n54\t  be enabled/configured as part of the distributed workloads stack.\n55\t- Validate gang-scheduling capability at the infrastructure level: pod groups\n56\t  are scheduled all-or-nothing in controlled tests.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- The coscheduling scheduler-plugin is packaged and deployable as part of the\n61\t  platform's distributed workloads stack.\n62\t- Given the plugin is deployed, when a pod group is scheduled, then the group\n63\t  is placed all-or-nothing in validation tests (zero partial placement).\n64\t- Given the plugin is deployed, when ordinary (non-gang) workloads are\n65\t  scheduled, then default scheduling behavior is unchanged.\n66\t- The plugin's deployment can be enabled, disabled, and configured through\n67\t  supported platform configuration.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- HLR-1 (P0, multi-node training jobs are admitted all-or-nothing): this epic\n72\t  provides the gang-scheduling infrastructure that enables HLR-1 in outcome B\n73\t  (scheduler-plugin required); the job-type admission integration that\n74\t  completes HLR-1 is carried by the follow-on epic in this branch.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b03e3fa461f4ed78","agent_id":"a0b58cf02cca6a57f","session_id":"e20e0106-1bbf-436d-84aa-f1899f83fce7","uuid":"9ab314c5-04ca-4243-8a5c-2cf7f68eda9a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:44:18.658Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae1aa398148a75fb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
